<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="6dc3d5de-30e1-5f3d-804f-5aa8a9224e74" activityNameId="5ba220cc-5a3d-5f05-89ed-96a09a392da7" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, nuclear, at power plant pressure water reactor</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, nuclear, at power plant pressure water reactor
The average burnup 42.5 MWd/kg heavy metal around year 2000 has been assumed representative for the lifetime of the modeled plant. The average burnup corresponds to an average enrichment of 3.8% U235 for fresh uranium fuel elements. Over the lifetime of the plant it can be assumed that approximately 10% of the energy will be produced by MOX fuel elements. Of total fuel elements 90% are assumed to be from fresh U (thus burdened by the full upstream chain), and 10% MOX (burdened by reprocessing). The utilisation factor for the infrastructure is the inverse of the total net electricity delivered in 40 years lifetime;
UUID: f70df649-dd9e-3fef-b46e-6a867c000041
The module includes fuel elements, chemicals, and diesel requirements as well as the relevant transport requirements. Water use (fresh and decarbonized) for cooling is included. Considered radioactive waste streams are: spent fuel to reprocessing and conditioning; operational low active waste for conditioning in the intermediate repository; and, contaminated waste from dismantling. Non-radioactive wastes are accounted for.
Location: Swiss data of one specific plant for requirements and all French PWRs for emissions.
Technology: Standard technology for commercial operation.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature and statistics of radioactive emissions. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_f70df649-dd9e-3fef-b46e-6a867c000041.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
